export anchor FocusColumnStyle:
    number: 178
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Focus column
    idea: The whole dashboard as one calm 720px column read top to bottom in priority order, a sentence that names what matters, then numbered sections set in a bookish serif on off-white paper with ink blue accents and rules instead of boxes.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #faf8f3, the off-white page
        ink: #1b2433, text, section rules and the nav top rule
        inkBlue: #1d3c78, the wordmark, links, figures, section numbers, the primary button, progress lines, this week bars and focus
        muted: #5b5f68, meta, captions, times and the date kicker
        rule: #d8d3c7, hairlines between rows and figures
        lastWeek: #8a8f9c, outlines of last week bars
        ok: #2f6b3a, On track text and check circle
        risk: #8a4a00, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #a3261b, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        Two stacks. Reading text uses Charter, Bitstream Charter, Iowan Old
        Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Georgia at 17px and 1.6. Meta,
        nav, buttons and labels use Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui,
        Roboto, Arial at 13 to 15px. The greeting is 44px serif bold at
        minus 0.02em, the lead 21px serif, section titles 22px serif bold,
        project names 19px serif bold, figures 40px serif regular in ink
        blue, and the date kicker and section numbers 13px sans caps tracked
        0.08 to 0.14em.
    layout:
        One centred column 720px wide with 16px side padding and nothing
        beside it. The masthead has the wordmark in ink blue, Bright bold
        and work italic, with a round outlined bell and Mara Okafor at
        right. Under it the six nav items run as one line of sans text links
        between a 2px ink rule above and a hairline below, Home underlined
        in ink blue. Then an underlined search field and a New project
        button on one line. The greeting follows with generous space, a caps
        date kicker, a 44px serif Good morning, Mara. and a lead sentence
        that starts with 4 tasks are overdue in red with a clock and names
        the behind and at risk projects. Five numbered sections follow, each
        titled under a 2px ink rule. 01 Needs attention lists the overdue
        tasks, Billing migration and Mobile app 2.0 with icons in the margin
        and open task counts. 02 This week shows the four figures as large
        serif numbers in a row split by hairlines. 03 All projects is an
        ordered list, most urgent first, with an index number, the serif
        name, the status at right, meta with category, tasks, due date and
        days left, and a 2px progress line. 04 Tasks completed opens with a
        sentence of the week totals over square outlined and solid bars. 05
        Recent activity puts the time in a left margin column. A closing
        line ends the page. Below 760px figures go two by two and the margin
        times move under each entry.
    spacing: An 8px unit with a reading rhythm. 56px above the greeting, 48px between sections, 16px row padding.
    density: Low. One column, one thing after another, wide line height.
    corners: Square. Only the bell, avatar and buttons at 2px or round.
    borders: Rules only. A 2px ink rule over each section and the nav, 1px warm hairlines between rows, an underline for the search field.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.6px stroke, 18px, set in the text or in a 28px left
        margin. Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
        risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
        with the word.
    focus: A 2px ink blue outline offset 3px on every control and field.
    tone: Written and calm, in full sentences such as Billing migration is 30% done with 28 tasks open and 20 days to go.
